$0$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,border:solid 1pt]{\\phantom{\\textrm{odd}}}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\textrm{True}=1$ and $\\textrm{False}=0.$ \n\nAlso, the Peirce arrow $x_1 \\downarrow x_2$ is true if and only if both $x_1$ and $x_2$ are false ($0$).\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Boolean function is the following: \n\n| $x_1$ | $x_2$ | $x_1 \\downarrow x_2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}$ |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec136ed2-0cea-5d8f-a9bd-e3aab3b9d98c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Boolean Functions Given Logical Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6936a15b-a719-5c35-bb80-8b8eb34f6cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419710} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e83727-ddb4-5e55-adae-241fd6caece8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6936a15b-a719-5c35-bb80-8b8eb34f6cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419710} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df93ca0-d2fd-55be-92a5-46060b6f233d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97652f35-94aa-5875-b5b9-60d521639aa6" :